sequenceDiagram
    actor Main
    participant Game as SnakeGame
    participant Snake as Snake
    participant Policy as FoodGrowthPolicy

    Main->>Game: move RIGHT, snake eats food and grows to length 2
    Game->>Policy: shouldGrow next head
    Policy-->>Game: true
    Game->>Snake: wouldCollide next head, grow equals true
    Snake-->>Game: false
    Game->>Snake: move next head, grow equals true, tail is kept
    Game-->>Main: score 1

    Main->>Game: move LEFT, head returns to the current tail cell
    Game->>Policy: shouldGrow next head
    Policy-->>Game: false
    Game->>Snake: wouldCollide next head, grow equals false
    Note over Snake: next head equals the current tail, and the tail is about to vacate this move, so this is not a collision
    Snake-->>Game: false
    Game->>Snake: move next head, grow equals false, tail is popped
    Game-->>Main: score 1, game continues

    Note over Main,Policy: the practice code checked occupancy before knowing whether the tail would vacate, so this exact reversal was wrongly treated as game over
